    "real_programs": "All real-program regressions are within the same-binary paired instruction noise. Zod improves by 0.03116%, exceeding its 0.02337% paired floor; further address controls below bound the effect.",
    "zod_mechanism": "Linked image/address layout changes existing address-keyed lookup/probing paths. Inference: pointer-hash probe variation is a plausible specific source, not isolated to an individual table. No byte constructors occur in the Zod hot schema loop, so this is not claimed as a birth-brand optimization of that loop.",
    "zod_evidence": "An unchanged main binary varies by 0.08028% with ASLR enabled (n=5), larger than the B5 shift; arm distributions overlap. Recompiling main produces the identical SHA256. THP-off keeps full/minor counts at 0/75 and the small instruction improvement, excluding a huge-page or collection-count explanation.",
    "kernels": "Instruction reductions are at most 551 instructions per complete run. Removed birth/view rebrand work and changed linked-image/startup code are bounded fixed costs; generated inner-loop codegen was not changed. The micro differences are not claimed as throughput gains.",
    "rss": "No median real-program RSS delta is near 2 MiB. Worker scheduling already varies live allocation/RSS and instruction counts on the same binary. Zod has identical anonymous RSS and huge-page sampling; its 64 KiB RSS difference is file-backed. The buffer-readwrite micro has +508 KiB RSS. The original 20 ms smaps sampler missed its peak, so its zero huge-page samples are not proof of THP absence. A 0.5 ms control sees 4 MiB huge pages on both arms, with median anonymous RSS 6960/6976 KiB and file RSS 7032/8368 KiB: resident image-page variation dominates. THP-off gives median sampled RSS 9900/10100 KiB, AnonHugePages=0 on all trials. No new retained allocation or collection regime was introduced."
